{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.FrobeniusDualH3","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.FrobeniusDualH3","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Matrix.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.NonsingularInverse","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.frobeniusDual_pairing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.frobeniusDual_pairing","kind":"theorem","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/frobenius-dual-h3.lean#L36-L43","doc":"Defining property of the Frobenius dual: pairing `K^∨` back\nthrough the Gram matrix `G` recovers the original coordinates,\nprovided `G` is invertible (`⟨K^∨, b_·⟩_F = c`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.frobeniusDual","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.frobeniusDual","kind":"def","line":31,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/frobenius-dual-h3.lean#L31-L34","doc":"The **Frobenius dual** coordinate vector `K^∨ = c · G⁻¹` of a\nstate with coordinate vector `c`, relative to the Gram matrix `G`. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:frobenius-dual-h3","label":"def:frobenius-dual-h3","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/frobenius-dual-h3.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}